<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    FLAMEFANG_SNAKE_REBIRTH_1 — owner sheet note, 2026-09-16, verbatim:
    "rename this to Flamefang and make it venomous." Postdates and
    supersedes BOOMSNAKE_CUT_CONFLICT_1 (2026-09-14), which had evicted
    GR_Boomsnake from the Pyrelands after finding no ruling had ever
    restored it post-BOOM_FAMILY_CUT_1 — see WildAnimals_Pyrelands.xml's
    header for the full timeline. GR_Boomsnake's ThingDef cut is reversed
    (Cherry Picker) and it is back in the_pyrelands.json's fauna array under
    this new identity.

    Structure copied from RazorjackIdentity_Sytheclaw.xml (same pattern: a
    PatchOperationFindMod on the donor mod wrapping a PatchOperationSequence
    of label/description Replaces): defName stays GR_Boomsnake because it is
    the DONOR mod's (Vanilla Genetics Expanded) own defName — this patch
    matches the donor's live def by that name and cannot rename it without
    absorbing the def outright, which is out of scope here; this is not a
    naming-scheme gate (NAMING_SCHEME_EXECUTION_1 closed 2026-08-31, no gate
    remains) — this patch moves only the player-facing identity (labels +
    description) into our own modspace. No art restyle
    here (out of scope per this item's own note 6 — the existing
    BoomsnakeArtOverride wiring from 2026-09-14 stays as-is). Venom mechanism
    is a separate patch, Patches/FlamefangVenom.xml.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Vanilla Genetics Expanded</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="GR_Boomsnake"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>flamefang</label></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="GR_Boomsnake"]/description</xpath>
          <value><description>A serpent of the burning grass that reads a fire front the way other things read a scent trail. It beds down in the smoldering root-mat ahead of the flames and waits, coiled tight, until the heat rolls over it and drives every small thing running — then it strikes from the ash. Its bite carries a burning venom that keeps working long after the fangs are gone, a second, slower fire under the skin.</description></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="GR_Boomsnake"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>flamefang</label></value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
